# ledger-invariants.baseline — THE KNOWN, ARGUED FINDING SET OF nexus/
#
# WHAT THIS FILE IS. One `CLASS<TAB>path` row per (class, file) pair that
# `ledgerguard --root nexus` reports today. It is read by
# `.softhouse/guards/drive-red-ledger-invariants.sh`, whose CONTROL used to be
# "the unmodified tree must exit 0" and cannot be any more: the tree is RED by a
# recorded decision (T502 / T505 / T514 / T516 — the four `loanproduct` schedule-intermediate
# sites stay refused until a go/types reachability discriminator exists).
#
# WHAT IT IS NOT. It is NOT an exemption, a waiver or a suppression. The guard's exit
# code is untouched by it: `check-ledger-invariants.sh` still refuses, the bar is still
# red, and nothing in this file is consulted when a finding is decided. Its only reader
# is the drive-red CONTROL, which asserts the set is EXACTLY this — no more, no fewer.
#
# BOTH DIRECTIONS FAIL, and the second one is the point:
#   * a NEW (class, file) pair appears  -> a violation entered a file that had none;
#   * a LISTED pair DISAPPEARS          -> a known violation was silenced, and silencing
#                                          one must be an explicit edit to this file,
#                                          reviewed like any other diff.
# The second direction is the one that catches a rename that turns the bar green while
# changing nothing — the move T502 was sent to make and refused to make.
#
# GRANULARITY, AND ITS RESIDUAL, STATED. Rows carry NO LINE NUMBERS, because line
# numbers drift on every unrelated edit to nexus/ and a control that fails on drift is a
# control that gets deleted. The cost is real and is not hidden: a SECOND finding of an
# already-listed class in an already-listed file does not move this set. That case is
# still caught by the guard itself, which prints every finding with its position and
# exits non-zero; this file is a no-silent-CHANGE check, not the guard.
#
# HOW TO REGENERATE (and read the diff before you commit it):
#   ledgerguard --root nexus | grep -E '^  \[' \
#     | sed -E 's/^  \[([A-Z0-9-]+)\] ([^:]+):.*/\1\t\2/' | sort -u
#
# Measured by T509 at 42 findings across 14 pairs. RE-MEASURED after the savings and
# working-capital repairs landed: 34 findings across the 9 pairs below. The five rows
# those repairs cleared were REMOVED IN THE SAME COMMIT that carries them, which is the
# only admissible way for a row to leave this file (see the REPAIRED block at the end).
#
# --- the four loanproduct schedule intermediates: a KNOWN, ARGUED, TEST-PINNED red ---
#     Not ledger balances on the two legs that survive (T516): LEG 1 parity — applying
#     I-3's remedy changes the money, because the oracle refreshes outstandingLoanBalance
#     only at explicit sweeps and reads it stale in between (executable, not argued); and
#     LEG 2 reachability — the value reaches no journal entry, GL posting or column any
#     aggregate reads as an account balance, its persistence being a closed loop written by
#     the projection and reloaded as the same projection's starting state. They stay
#     refused because the only mechanism that could distinguish them soundly is LEG 2's
#     go/types reachability discriminator, which does not exist yet, and the
#     persistence-surface heuristic proposed instead was MEASURED being defeated by one
#     `git mv` (T505 MAJOR-1).
I3-COMPOSITE-BALANCE	internal/apps/loanproduct/interestperiod.go
I3-COMPOSITE-BALANCE	internal/apps/loanproduct/repaymentperiod.go
I3-FIELD-WRITE	internal/apps/loanproduct/interestperiod.go
I3-FIELD-WRITE	internal/apps/loanproduct/repaymentperiod.go
#
# --- found by T509's widening; each needs an owner, none is cleared by this file ---
#     loan/charge.go         AmountOutstanding, the port of m_loan_charge.amount_outstanding_derived
#                            [LoanCharge.java:108].
#     loanschedule/emi.go    the roll-forward that is the twin of the loanproduct sites and
#                            shipped GREEN for two months because it is spelled outstandingMinor.
#     exemption_test.go      a test FIXTURE assigning OutstandingPrincipalMinor. CANNOT-CATCH
#                            item 8: tests are inspected, not exempted.
I3-FIELD-WRITE	internal/apps/loan/charge.go
I3-FIELD-WRITE	internal/apps/loanschedule/conformance/exemption_test.go
I3-FIELD-WRITE	internal/apps/loanschedule/emi.go
#
# --- REPAIRED, and therefore removed. Five rows, verified BEFORE removal ---
#     A row may leave this file only when the write path it names is GONE, never when the
#     guard merely stops seeing it. The guard cannot tell those apart — its detection
#     surface is the NAME — so each removal below was checked by hand against the tree:
#
#     savings/postgres.go     I3-FIELD-WRITE, I3-SQL-BALANCE   removed
#     savings/summary.go      I3-FIELD-WRITE                   removed
#       No INSERT or UPDATE in postgres.go reaches a balance-named column. The balance is
#       now produced by a value-returning fold over the transaction list,
#       `AccountBalanceOf(txns []SavingsAccountTransaction) MinorUnits` [summary.go:228],
#       with `RunningBalancesOf` [:421] and `HoldNetRunningBalancesOf` [:504] beside it.
#       Nothing persists their result. Landed by 78a17873 (T501), 5c4233fc (T510, the fold
#       learns about reversals) and 84dc208e / 738282a6 (T515, the reviewed rework).
#       6701d9d5 states the six cleared findings; 93cc16c9 reverted the FIRST T501 attempt,
#       which is why the repair is credited to the merged softhouse branch and not to it.
#
#     workingcapital/postgres.go  I3-SQL-BALANCE-TABLE, OPAQUE-SQL   removed
#       m_wc_loan_balance keeps no write path: 2723b086 makes it a READ MODEL. The
#       thirteen columns that never said "balance" are now computed per call on value
#       receivers — TotalOutstanding, PrincipalOutstanding, FeeOutstanding,
#       PenaltyOutstanding [workingcapital/balance.go:45-70]. ApplyDisbursement [:37] takes
#       a pointer receiver, but mutates an in-memory projection that no INSERT reads; it is
#       the projection-intermediate case, not an authoritative stored balance.
#       The OPAQUE-SQL row went with it: the spliced column list routed through
#       InsertReturningInt64 that T506 F-6 flagged is no longer built.
#
#     The nine rows above this block are UNCHANGED and remain refused.

# --- ADDED when the promotion harnesses landed. Three rows, all TEST FIXTURES ---
#     Same class as the loanschedule/conformance/exemption_test.go row above, and pinned
#     for the same stated reason: CANNOT-CATCH item 8 — tests are INSPECTED, not exempted.
#     The guard's detection surface is the NAME, and these three name a balance in a
#     REQUEST struct that a pure computation reads FROM:
#
#       loan/conformance/conformance_test.go:74,343
#         &RepaymentRequest{Outstanding: AllocationMoney{...}} in repaymentProbe and
#         TestAdmitDefaultDeny — the outstanding amount a repayment is allocated against.
#       savings/conformance/conformance_test.go:73,238
#         &DailyInterestRequest{BalanceMinor: "100000"} in dailyInterestProbe — the
#         balance the daily accrual is computed FROM.
#
#     None of these is a DERIVED balance being written. Each is an INPUT to a computation,
#     constructed in test code, never persisted, and never read back as an account balance.
#     I-3 forbids deriving a balance and then storing it; it does not forbid naming the
#     input a calculation consumes.
#
#     REMOVAL CONDITION: if any of these fixtures is ever changed so the value it carries
#     is written to a persistence boundary rather than passed to a pure function, the row
#     stops being justified and the finding becomes real. Repair it then; do not keep it.
I3-COMPOSITE-BALANCE	internal/apps/loan/conformance/conformance_test.go
I3-COMPOSITE-BALANCE	internal/apps/savings/conformance/conformance_test.go
I3-FIELD-WRITE	internal/apps/savings/conformance/conformance_test.go
#
# --- REPAIRED and removed: the two investor rows. Verified BEFORE removal ---
#     These two rows covered TEN findings — five I3-SQL-BALANCE at the INSERT and five
#     I3-FIELD-WRITE at the read-back — and they are the first rows in this file to leave it
#     because the defect was FIXED rather than argued.
#
#     The guard refused when they vanished, which is the ratchet's second direction working:
#     a repair and a rename are indistinguishable to a NAME-based detector, so the guard
#     demands the removal be a visible diff. This is that diff.
#
#     WHAT WAS REPAIRED (investor/postgres.go, commits 8ad136b3 and e8dececf):
#       Insert       stopped writing the loan-outstanding snapshot into the five
#                    *_outstanding_derived columns of m_external_asset_owner_transfer_details
#       loadDetails  stopped SELECTing them back into the aggregate's balance fields
#     Either half alone fixes nothing: without the first a write path remains; without the
#     second a decoded balance is still trusted.
#
#     CHECKED BY HAND before these rows were removed, because the guard cannot tell a repair
#     from a rename:
#       * no `*_outstanding_derived` reference remains anywhere in the file
#       * the only lines matching "INSERT/SELECT ... balance" are the COMMENTS at :26 and :37
#         asserting no such statement exists
#       * ExternalAssetOwnerTransferDetails SURVIVES — 11 references, 8 [VERIFIED:] citations.
#         A previous task in this programme made a finding vanish by deleting the ported type
#         and its citation; this count fell because the write path is gone, not the evidence
#       * FindByID and FindByLoanID still exist — the stored balance went, the API did not
#       * INV-01-transfer-read still grades parity_pass=1
#
#     The port's own doc.go already stated the rule postgres.go was breaking: total outstanding
#     "is DERIVED from the four component buckets, never stored independently".
#
#     RE-ADD CONDITION: if any statement in investor/postgres.go ever names one of those six
#     columns again, these rows come back in the same commit that reintroduces it.

# --- ADDED with the workingcapital balance seam. Two rows, harness evaluator ---
#     workingcapital/conformance/impl.go:127  &DetailExpect{Balance: BalanceExpect{...}}
#     workingcapital/conformance/impl.go:184  d.Balance.TotalOutstanding = ...
#
#     These are the CONFORMANCE EVALUATOR, not the port. Grading a balance read-back
#     requires computing a balance to compare against the observed one, so the evaluator
#     necessarily names balance fields. Same class as the loan/savings conformance_test.go
#     rows above and CANNOT-CATCH item 8 — instruments are INSPECTED, not exempted.
#
#     CHECKED before recording: impl.go contains no database/sql or platform/postgres
#     import and no INSERT/UPDATE statement; DetailExpect and BalanceExpect have no reader
#     outside workingcapital/conformance. The value is compared and discarded. Nothing
#     derived here reaches a persistence boundary.
#
#     Distinguish this from investor/postgres.go, whose two rows LEFT this file today: that
#     was the PORT's own persistence layer writing and reading back a stored balance. This
#     is a test instrument with no persistence at all — the same distinction that made
#     loan/charge.go's eleven sites benign and investor's ten sites real.
#
#     REMOVAL CONDITION: if the workingcapital conformance package ever gains a persistence
#     import or a reader outside itself, these rows stop being justified and the findings
#     become real.
I3-COMPOSITE-BALANCE	internal/apps/workingcapital/conformance/impl.go
I3-FIELD-WRITE	internal/apps/workingcapital/conformance/impl.go
